one selector, two element widths, and this is the other side of the pair

NSFont writes NSGlyph, which is NSUInteger and EIGHT bytes. KTFont answers the SAME selector,
getGlyphs:forCharacters:length:, and writes CGGlyph, which is TWO. An attributed string built through
CoreText legitimately carries a KTFont under NSFontAttributeName, because kCTFontAttributeName IS
NSFontAttributeName, so this layout manager is handed both kinds and assumed one.

Two byte elements written into an eight byte array leave the first slot holding four packed
neighbours and every later slot untouched. The layout that comes out is nonsense, and what it looks
like is a twelve character label drawn as one character at a width that has nothing to do with the
string. Money Manager EX drew its whole startup screen that way: O, N, O, U, U, Wi, Fm.

The element width is read from the METHOD rather than the class, which is the rule the fix on the
other side of this pair already uses in CTFontGetGlyphsForCharacters:

  method_copyArgumentType(class_getInstanceMethod([font class], @selector(...)), 2)

and ^S means CGGlyph *. A narrow callee gets a bounce buffer that is widened afterwards; a wide one
is called directly and costs nothing.

MEASURED, on the same nine labels, before and after:

  "Open Last Opened Database"   183.00 -> 159.00   25 characters
  "New Database"                 49.00 ->  81.00   12
  "Open Existing Database"       41.00 -> 132.00   22
  "User Interface Language"      46.00 -> 135.00   23
  "User Manual"                  46.00 ->  70.00   11
  "Website"                      48.00 ->  44.00    7
  "Forum"                        37.00 ->  35.00    5

Every after value is about 6.3 per character; not one of the before values was. The buttons wx sized
from those measurements went from 60 points wide to 163, and every label now reads in full.

The trace that found it is kept: CIDER_TRACE_TEXT prints the font CLASS, the glyph range, the
character count and how many glyphs came back as nothing.

IT IS NOT IN NSGlyphGenerator, which is where I put it first. That class is dead code in this port
and a probe inside it printed nothing for an application that plainly draws text; the control was
that the probe string WAS in the built binary. The two live call sites are both in NSLayoutManager.

